<title>SINGAPORE: Datacraft 1995/96 net profit up 40.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Datacraft 1995/96 net profit up 40.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telecommunications and computer network company Datacraft Asia Ltd said on Monday it was restating its 1995/96 financial results to reflect the purchase of a previous associate company.</p>
<p>The move followed the approval by Datacraft shareholders on Monday of the 100 percent purchase of Datacraft New Zealand from Australian parent company Datacraft Ltd.</p>
<p>Results for year to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in millions of US dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				6.68 vs  4.76</p>
<p>    Dividend (Singapore cents)	  0.73 vs   NA</p>
<p>    Group shr (US cents)		  3.7  vs  3.1</p>
<p>    Group shr fully diluted (US cts)  3.6  vs  3.0</p>
<p>    Turnover				 86.72 vs 63.55</p>
<p>    Operating profit		     10.73 vs  8.05</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		    0.21 vs  0.30</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)		2.27 vs  1.57</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			  8.25 vs  6.18</p>
<p>    Tax					 1.53 vs  1.37</p>
<p>    Minorities loss			 0.04 vs  0.04</p>
<p>    Dividend pay date:   December 20, 1996</p>
<p>Last day books open: December 10, 1996</p>
</text>
